# API route authentication

When adding or changing `src/app/api/**/route.ts`:

1. Call `requireAuth(request)` at the start of each handler unless the route is intentionally public.
2. Public exceptions (no `requireAuth`): `auth/login`, `auth/logout`, `auth/me`, `auth/[...nextauth]`, `register`, and read-only `api/route.ts` health if kept.
3. Dev-only routes must still use `requireAuth` and guard with `NODE_ENV !== 'production'` (see `api/dev/prisma-studio`).
4. On auth failure: `if ("error" in auth) return auth.error`.
5. Scope data to `auth.userId` — never trust client-supplied user ids for ownership.

Do not add new unauthenticated write endpoints without explicit product approval.
